WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.962 --> 00:00:03.420
AGV: Today we're talking about
machine learning and contact

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:06.510
centers, Workflows, and N2 VMs.

00:00:06.510 --> 00:00:09.660
I'm AGV, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.760
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.610
Speaker ID brings Google's
speech identification

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.000
technology directly to Google
Cloud customers and our contact

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.080
center partners.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:22.140
Instead of subjugating
callers to tedious

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.470
and circuitous authentication
processes, such as phone trees

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:29.010
or menus with speaker IDs,
our customers and partners

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.100
can now initiate service using
the most intuitive interface

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:32.910
of all--

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.140
voice.

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.270
With Workflows,
developers can easily

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.370
orchestrate various
services together

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:42.340
on Google Cloud or
third-party APIs.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.220
And with callbacks, the
execution of a Workflow

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:48.340
can wait until it receives a
call to a specific callback

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.060
endpoint.

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.340
Check out the blog
for examples and how

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.010
to use the helpful new feature.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:58.330
We are also expanding our N2 VM
family machine-type offering,

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:01.720
which will now offer our largest
Intel-based, general purpose,

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.520
pre-defined machines to date.

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:06.910
For scale-up workloads, that
can benefit from a higher number

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.170
of threads.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:12.310
We are also increasing the N2
custom machine-types maximum,

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:14.560
offering a compelling
upgrade path

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.430
from first-generation
general purpose N1 machines.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:20.957
Check out the blog
to learn more.

00:01:20.957 --> 00:01:23.040
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.980
or see a full list, we
have several lovely links.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.980
And optionally, if you would
like to leave us a comment

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.480
or tweet us, please do.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.690
We'll see you in the Cloud.

